{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/936099-two-different-visions","id":936099,"title":"Two different visions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-23T08:43:32-07:00","id":936099,"title":"Two different visions?","content":"So, I've noticed something very, very odd about Beast. On one hand, you have the vision of Beasts being awesome at what they do and being awesome for it. On the other hand, you have sections of the book that paint neither Beasts nor Heroes as being right for doing what they do most commonly (See: Sidebar on Page 202 the quote about being a Beast or Hero is what you make of it) and ultimately implying that the, &quot;Lessons&quot; Beasts impart are flimsy justifications for being a solidly terrible person as opposed to being metal versions of Dickens' Ghosts of Christmas. So I'm trying to figure something out. Which theme ultimately, are the writers trying to communicate here as the dominant approach? Certainly there's a degree of subjective material but... What IS Beast about, if we have conflicting evidence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2532-blitzkitty","name":"BlitzKitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2532_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T08:56:55-07:00","id":936103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlitzKitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/936099-two-different-visions#post936099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and being awesome for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how you mean this, you're either reading something into it that's not there or observing a trend that also exists in the 2e corebooks for Vampire and Werewolf, wherein the writing generally doesn't shy away from the notion that a character might find existence as a supernatural being enjoyable/compelling/&quot;awesome.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> flimsy justifications for being a solidly terrible person </div> </div> </div>Not what a cultural exhortation to keep the consequences of your actions as an easily-notorious dream-monster in mind means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which theme ultimately, are the writers trying to communicate here as the dominant approach? Certainly there's a degree of subjective material but... What IS Beast about, if we have conflicting evidence? </div> </div> </div>Engagement with community as self-exploration, exploration of how being a monster interferes with your ability to relate to people, and the necessity of acknowledging the darker side of humanity in a more direct fashion than the more unusual/abstracted drives of other gamelines, among other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}